This project uses the Developer Certificate of Origin (DCO), version 1.1:

https://developercertificate.org/

By submitting a contribution, certify that you have the right to submit
it under this project's MIT license. Add a Signed-off-by trailer to each
commit, using your real name and contact address:

    Signed-off-by: Your Name <you@example.org>

git commit -s adds the trailer. Read the complete DCO before signing.

Use SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT in source files. Keep dependencies small,
document operational behavior and test meaningful invariants: FIFO claims,
owner checks, process cleanup and archival verification.

Run:

    PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v

Changes to systemd integration also need a real user-service check. Use
an isolated database and a CPU-only test resource; never run a test on
someone else's GPU reservation or stop their processes.

Keep host configuration, credentials, databases, logs, checkpoints and
private experiment evidence outside the source tree.
Use generic deployment placeholders in public documentation. Never publish
personal machine names, filesystem layouts, network addresses or runtime
records without the owner's explicit approval. Review the full staged diff
and commit history for these details before publishing.

Describe substantial AI assistance in the pull request description.
Contributors remain responsible for understanding and testing their changes.
